        "summary":  "The Real-SWE benchmark tests AI coding agents on private production codebases from real companies, making data contamination less likely than benchmarks using public repos. Even the top performer, Claude Fable 5.1, scored only 38.8%, failing more than 60% of the time. Six of ten task categories posted success rates below 15%, with no model solving the analytics stream reducer task across 64 total attempts.",
