        "summary":  "Google demonstrated that combining the Antigravity Teamwork framework with Gemini 3.7 Flash enables autonomous AI agent teams to collaborate, critique, and iterate over hours or days on complex problems. The system solved seven open math research problems, built a functional RISC-V CPU simulator, and contributed performance improvements to established open-source libraries. Results showed 0.71% cycle alignment error in hardware simulation, indicating production-grade accuracy for mission-critical tasks.",
        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s multi-agent Teamwork framework marks a shift from single-model queries to sustained agent collaboration capable of research-grade problem-solving — a capability threshold relevant to enterprise R\u0026D and complex engineering workflows. Organizations should take note that multi-agent orchestration now demonstrably handles long-horizon tasks (hours to days) that single models cannot. The ROI case is emerging for applying these systems to complex software, scientific, and infrastructure challenges. The caveat: these demonstrations are on well-defined benchmark problems; enterprise deployment will require robust task scoping and failure-recovery design.",
