        "execSummary":  "Claude Opus 5.5 materially changes the enterprise cost-benefit equation for frontier AI deployment: frontier-class capability at a 40% cost reduction means organizations that previously reserved advanced models for high-value use cases can expand deployment to a broader set of workflows. The 85% reduction in boundary circumvention and best-ever safety audit scores make a compelling case for enterprises in regulated industries considering autonomous agent deployments. One early customer migrated 680,000 lines of code in under a day — a productivity benchmark that reframes build-vs-buy decisions for engineering-heavy organizations. The key watch-out: expanded autonomy requires mature governance; enterprises should invest in evaluation and monitoring infrastructure to match the model\u0027s new capability envelope.",
