        "theme":  "Platforms",
        "summary":  "AWS announced that Anthropic\u0027s Claude Opus 5, Claude Sonnet 5, and Claude Haiku 4.5 models are now available on Amazon Bedrock in India via geographic cross-region inference between Mumbai and Hyderabad regions. Indian enterprises can now process data locally within India while accessing advanced AI capabilities without managing regional capacity constraints independently. The service maintains zero data retention by default and routes requests only within India\u0027s two regions.",
        "execSummary":  "AWS has extended Claude model access to Indian enterprises through in-country inferencing, directly addressing data residency and sovereignty requirements that have blocked AI adoption in regulated Indian industries. This matters for enterprise AI strategy because data localization is a compliance prerequisite in financial services, healthcare, and government sectors across South Asia — not just a preference. The distributed inference across Mumbai and Hyderabad also provides throughput resilience during traffic peaks, reducing a key operational risk. Enterprises evaluating India expansion should note this requires explicit IAM permission configuration and SDK updates, and should confirm their specific compliance frameworks accept AWS\u0027s regional routing model.",
