        "summary":  "Dan Roberts outlines seven leadership competencies for IT executives navigating AI-driven transformation: Coherence, Communication, Currency, Confidence, Conviction, Courage, and Change. The framework draws on experiences from CIOs at BNY, Johnson \u0026 Johnson, Liberty Mutual, Cox Automotive, GSK, Cardinal Health, and Deluxe. Roberts frames disruption not as a periodic event but as the permanent operating environment for modern IT leaders.",
        "execSummary":  "As AI reshapes every function, the most decisive variable is leadership capability, not technology selection. This framework from CIOs across major enterprises argues that navigating AI transformation requires seven distinct competencies — from maintaining conviction under uncertainty to accelerating change adoption. For senior leaders, the practical takeaway is that AI strategy without cultural and communicative scaffolding routinely stalls at the pilot stage. The organizations represented here have operationalized these traits into governance and talent models worth benchmarking.",
