        "url":  "https://www.cio.com/article/4221996/how-roche-drives-ai-outcomes-in-a-changing-world.html",
        "date":  "2026-09-16",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Roche\u0027s Chief Digital and Technology Officer Wafaa Mamilli discusses how the company uses trusted data foundations, governance frameworks, and outcome-focused strategies to drive AI innovation across drug discovery, diagnostics, and patient care. Mamilli emphasizes that risk management in regulated healthcare environments demands particularly rigorous AI governance. The approach centers on outcome measurement rather than technology deployment milestones.",
        "execSummary":  "Roche\u0027s model offers a replicable blueprint for enterprises in regulated industries trying to scale AI responsibly: start with data trust, not model capability. Mamilli\u0027s emphasis on governance-first and outcome-focused measurement directly addresses the gap between AI pilots and production value. For customer-support and operations leaders, the implication is that AI ambition must be matched by data infrastructure investment and clear accountability frameworks. Healthcare\u0027s high-stakes environment makes Roche\u0027s caution instructive even for lower-risk enterprise contexts.",
