        "source":  "CIO Dive",
        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/capital-one-agentic-ai-strategy/831435/",
        "date":  "2026-09-28",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Capital One\u0027s VP of Enterprise AI Rashmi Shetty describes how the bank\u0027s agentic AI strategy is built on a robust data foundation and platform-first architecture. The bank has deployed both internal and external AI agents, including a Chat Concierge tool for car-buying assistance, with governance, observability, and human-in-the-loop controls for high-risk operations. Anthropic\u0027s Claude Agent SDK underpins part of the implementation.",
        "execSummary":  "Capital One\u0027s approach is one of the most detailed public blueprints for enterprise agentic AI at scale in a regulated environment. The platform-first, data-foundation principle directly addresses the most common failure mode in agentic deployments: agents that lack the context quality to act reliably. For customer-support and operations leaders, the human-in-the-loop controls for high-risk decisions are the critical design choice to replicate. The Anthropic dependency also signals that enterprise-grade agent SDKs are now a real procurement consideration alongside model selection.",
