        "date":  "2026-09-28",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Nvidia launched the Open Agent Safety Platform, featuring OpenShell for secure runtime boundaries and Sentry for continuous monitoring running on BlueField-4 DPUs. Over 100 organizations including Microsoft, Salesforce, Anthropic, and OpenAI are participating in the platform. Analysts caution that a single unified governance solution cannot address all enterprise scenarios and that the platform primarily protects agents running within Nvidia\u0027s controlled infrastructure.",
        "execSummary":  "Nvidia\u0027s move to embed agent governance at the silicon layer represents a significant escalation in the AI safety arms race — and a strategic land-grab for infrastructure ownership in agentic deployments. For enterprise leaders, the partnership roster of 100+ organizations signals this will become a de facto standard for on-prem and hybrid agentic workloads. The critical caveat is analyst-noted coverage gaps: this platform does not govern cloud-native agents outside Nvidia\u0027s stack. Procurement teams should assess whether their agentic architectures are Nvidia-centric enough to benefit.",
        "vendorLean":  "Nvidia — positive",
